WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.425
Each degree has sixty minutes.

2
00:00:02.675 --> 00:00:15.525
The training chart’s scales divide each minute into tenths, so positions are written in degrees, minutes and tenths of a minute: forty-one degrees, eighteen point five minutes means eighteen and a half minutes.

3
00:00:15.775 --> 00:00:20.675
Don’t confuse that with eighteen minutes, fifty seconds, an older format.

4
00:00:20.925 --> 00:00:27.200
Count the small tick marks carefully, since scales at different latitudes may be divided differently.

5
00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:33.250
Always write latitude first, with north or south, then longitude, with east or west.
